// fixed is held by it, and a change on one of its instances goes back. Two that disagree are a
// conflict. Each known size then gives a scale; one no different is left (szW SZSAME); a scale
// out of range or a box off the screen is refused. A free Z's scalar reads its instance's size.
// szStepOv makes each new scale's words ready, its master's record resident each time, and then
// sets them all, keeping the words before in uSz; refused, each instance goes back, the source
// to szPrev (szDirty) and a new entry out of the table (szNew), the word why shown. Going back
// is not refused in turn (szRet). szBackOv puts uSz back for Undo. The sizes are set as scApply
